// Test: bugfixes/return_any_unboxes_to_concrete
// Regression: CODEGEN-RETURN-ANY-NOT-UNBOXED-TO-CONCRETE-RETURN-TYPE
//
// Before the fix: a function declared to return a concrete type (e.g. `string`)
// that returned the result of a Call producing `any` (e.g. `json.get`) emitted
// the raw boxed-Any wrapper pointer at the WASM return instruction. The caller
// treated those bytes as a length-prefixed Clean string, reading the type-tag
// word at offset 0 as the string length and the inner-pointer word at offset 4
// as the first 4 bytes of string content — producing nonsensical output like
// "H  " for a "Basics" result.
//
// The bug existed in 0.30.372 → 0.30.379. It was masked in production by the
// CMP-SSR-MALLOC-OOM-PAGE-RENDER OOM (page handlers errored before reaching
// the empty-data code path). When the OOM was fixed in 0.30.379 the empty
// strings surfaced as empty SSR output.
//
// Fix: in `TastStatement::Return` MIR lowering, mirror the existing
// `needs_unboxing` check from the `VariableDeclaration` path. When the
// function's declared return type is concrete (string/integer/number/boolean)
// and the expression evaluates to Any, emit `UnboxAnyToConcrete` before the
// return, dispatching on the function's declared return type.
//
// Expected output:
//   Basics
//   6

start:
	Demo d = Demo("{\"title\":\"Basics\"}")
	string r = d.slug()
	printl(r)
	printl(r.length().toString())

class Demo
	string sectionJson
	constructor(string s)
		sectionJson = s
	functions:
		public:
			string slug()
				return json.get(sectionJson, "title")
